{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is plausible, but the current row relies on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field. Use FDA/openFDA or FDA accessdata label metadata instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"zonisamide","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"zonisamide","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies the active ingredient/generic as zonisamide.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name was verified. ZNS is an abbreviation/search alias, not a generic name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"ZNS","rationale":"RCT evidence summaries commonly abbreviate zonisamide as ZNS, so this is a useful PubMed/search alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Desizon; Zonegran; Zonisade","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Desizon; Zonegran; Zonisade","rationale":"Zonegran and Zonisade are verified by FDA labeling. Desizon was not verified from the trusted sources available in this audit, so retain only if a trusted eMC/SmPC or EMA source is added. Do not add 'Zonisamide' as a trade name; it is the generic name, not a proprietary name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"insufficient_evidence","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labels exist for Zonegran capsules and Zonisade oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Capsule; oral suspension","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Capsule; oral suspension","rationale":"FDA labeling supports capsule and oral suspension formulations.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"400 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"600 mg/day; usual target 400 mg/day, with labeling noting no evidence of increasing response above 400 mg/day","rationale":"Current FDA Zonisade labeling states patients tolerating 400 mg daily may be increased to a maximum dosage of 600 mg daily, while also noting controlled trials show no increased response above 400 mg/day.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"100 mg/day starting; effective maintenance commonly 100-400 mg/day","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"100 mg/day starting; effective maintenance commonly 100-400 mg/day","rationale":"FDA labeling supports 100 mg daily initial dosing and titration to 400 mg daily; RCT evidence also reports efficacy at 100 mg/day in Faught2001.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Adults: 100-400 mg/day once daily or divided","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Adults: 100-400 mg/day once daily or divided; selected patients may be increased to 600 mg/day per FDA labeling","rationale":"FDA labeling supports once- or twice-daily administration, initial 100 mg/day, titration to 400 mg/day, and possible increase to 600 mg/day.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"50-70 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"50-70 h","rationale":"FDA labeling reports plasma elimination half-life of about 63 hours; enzyme-inducing AEDs shorten half-life.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver and renal excretion","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic metabolism with renal excretion","rationale":"FDA labeling states zonisamide is metabolized by N-acetyl-transferases and CYP3A4 and excreted primarily in urine as parent drug and glucuronide metabolite.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Not a major inducer/inhibitor; CYP3A4 substrate; weak carbonic anhydrase inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Not expected to affect other drugs via CYP450-mediated mechanisms; metabolized partly by CYP3A4; carbonic anhydrase inhibitor","rationale":"FDA labeling supports insignificant CYP inhibition, CYP3A4 metabolism, and carbonic anhydrase inhibition. The label does not frame the carbonic anhydrase effect as 'weak'.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Precise mechanism is unknown; in vitro data suggest sodium-channel blockade and reduced T-type calcium currents, with weak carbonic-anhydrase inhibition of uncertain therapeutic contribution.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Precise mechanism is unknown; in vitro data suggest sodium-channel blockade and reduced T-type calcium currents, with carbonic-anhydrase inhibition of uncertain therapeutic contribution.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the sodium-channel, T-type calcium-current, and carbonic-anhydrase statements; it does not use 'weak' for the carbonic-anhydrase effect.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Calcium channel / alpha-2-delta; Sodium channel","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"Calcium channel / T-type; Sodium channel; Carbonic anhydrase inhibitor","rationale":"Alpha-2-delta is not supported for zonisamide. FDA labeling supports sodium channels, T-type calcium currents, and carbonic anhydrase inhibition.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Focal; Generalized; Primary generalized tonic-clonic","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal/partial-onset seizures; generalized and primary generalized tonic-clonic use require an added trusted source or should be marked off-label/not verified","rationale":"FDA labeling supports adjunctive treatment of partial-onset seizures. The cited row sources do not verify generalized or primary generalized tonic-clonic use as a supported row fact.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00692003"]},{"current_value":"CNS: somnolence 17%, GI: anorexia 13%, CNS: dizziness 13%, neurologic: ataxia 6%, cognitive: abnormal thinking 6%, renal/metabolic: kidney stones 4% over development program","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: somnolence 17%, GI: anorexia 13%, CNS: dizziness 13%, neurologic: ataxia 6%, cognitive: confusion/difficulty concentrating/difficulty with memory 6%, renal/metabolic: kidney stones 4% over development program","rationale":"FDA labeling verifies somnolence, anorexia, dizziness, and ataxia percentages. The 6% cognitive events are reported as confusion, difficulty concentrating, and difficulty with memory rather than the exact term 'abnormal thinking'.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No FDA QT-prolongation warning identified in reviewed FDA labeling","rationale":"The reviewed FDA labels do not establish a clinically meaningful QT effect, but absence of a QT warning is narrower than proof of no clinically meaningful QT effect.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"2000","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2000","rationale":"FDA labeling states Initial U.S. Approval: 2000, and the original Zonegran FDA labeling text is dated March 27, 2000.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Current ASM for focal/partial seizures; also used off-label for migraine/weight-related indications in some settings.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Current ASM for adjunctive treatment of focal/partial-onset seizures; non-epilepsy off-label uses require added trusted sources if retained.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports partial-onset seizure use. The migraine/weight-related off-label statement is not supported by the row's named trusted evidence sources.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]}],"generic_name":"zonisamide","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"10.7-31 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Guerrini2013 zonisamide target 8 mg/kg/day 19%; Lu2011 zonisamide 400 mg/day 20.5%; Brodie2005 zonisamide 500 mg/day 31%; Sackellares2004 zonisamide titrated 400-600 mg/day 10.7%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"10.7-31 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Guerrini2013 zonisamide target 8 mg/kg/day 19%; Lu2011 zonisamide 400 mg/day 20.5%; Brodie2005 zonisamide 500 mg/day 31%; Sackellares2004 zonisamide titrated 400-600 mg/day 10.7%)","rationale":"The component differentials match extractable active-minus-placebo responder rates: Guerrini 50% vs 31%, Lu 56.5% vs 36.0%, Brodie 52.3% vs 21.3%, Sackellares 26.9% vs 16.2%.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23837461/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15660766/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15144425/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"31.5-34.9 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Brodie2005 zonisamide 500 mg/day 34.9%; Sackellares2004 zonisamide titrated 400-600 mg/day 33.6%; Faught2001 zonisamide 400 mg/day 31.5%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"31.5-34.9 % (arithmetic active-minus-placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Brodie2005 51.2% vs 16.3% = 34.9% [reported between-group estimate 31.2%]; Sackellares2004 28.9% vs -4.7% = 33.6%; Faught2001 40.5% vs 9.0% = 31.5%)","rationale":"The arithmetic active-minus-placebo values are supported, but Brodie2005 also reports a between-group estimate of 31.2%, so the row should clarify arithmetic versus reported estimate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15660766/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15144425/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11723262/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"3.8 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential extractable from Lu2011 pooled zonisamide 300-400 mg/day: 3/52 [5.8%] vs 1/50 [2.0%]; no dose-specific 400 mg/day seizure-freedom differential extractable from included abstracts/evidence summaries)","rationale":"NCBI evidence tables report Lu2011 seizure freedom as 3/52 for zonisamide versus 1/50 for placebo, so the current NR statement is not fully correct.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lu2011|3.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/|104","rationale":"A pooled Lu2011 seizure-freedom differential is extractable, although not dose-specific to the 400 mg/day arm.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"ZNS","reason":"ZNS is a common zonisamide abbreviation in RCT evidence summaries.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"400 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"600 mg/day; usual target 400 mg/day, with labeling noting no evidence of increasing response above 400 mg/day","reason":"Current FDA labeling permits increase to 600 mg/day in selected patients tolerating 400 mg/day.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Calcium channel / alpha-2-delta; Sodium channel","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"Calcium channel / T-type; Sodium channel; Carbonic anhydrase inhibitor","reason":"Alpha-2-delta is not supported; FDA labeling supports T-type calcium currents, sodium channels, and carbonic anhydrase inhibition.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"3.8 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential extractable from Lu2011 pooled zonisamide 300-400 mg/day: 3/52 [5.8%] vs 1/50 [2.0%]; no dose-specific 400 mg/day seizure-freedom differential extractable from included abstracts/evidence summaries)","reason":"Lu2011 reports extractable seizure-freedom counts in NCBI evidence tables.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lu2011|3.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/|104","reason":"Adds the extractable Lu2011 pooled seizure-freedom differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Guerrini2013","pmid":"23837461","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"Correct PMID for adjunctive zonisamide in pediatric partial epilepsy; randomized phase III, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multicenter trial; responder differential 50% vs 31% = 19%.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23837461/"},{"label":"Lu2011","pmid":"21166480","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"Correct PMID for adjunctive zonisamide in adult refractory partial-onset epilepsy; PubMed verifies randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design, zonisamide 300-400 mg/day, and placebo control.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/"},{"label":"Brodie2005","pmid":"15660766","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"Correct PMID for zonisamide dose-ranging adjunctive RCT; NCBI evidence summary verifies randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design, 351 randomized, 100/300/500 mg/day arms, and placebo control.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15660766/"},{"label":"Sackellares2004","pmid":"15144425","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"Correct PMID for adjunctive zonisamide in refractory partial seizures; NCBI evidence summary verifies randomized placebo-controlled design, 152 subjects, titration to 400-600 mg/day, and placebo control.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15144425/"},{"label":"Faught2001","pmid":"11723262","proposed_action":"Keep","rationale":"Correct PMID for randomized double-blind placebo-controlled adjunctive zonisamide trial in refractory partial-onset seizures; NCBI evidence summary verifies 203 randomized and 400 mg/day target comparisons versus placebo.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11723262/"},{"label":"Schmidt1993","pmid":"8325280","proposed_action":"Keep in RCT links; do not use for max-dose outcome rollups unless dose/outcome extraction is explicitly documented","rationale":"Correct PMID for European double-blind placebo-controlled zonisamide add-on trial. NCBI evidence summary verifies randomized trial and placebo control but dose-specific maximum-effect outcome values are not suitable for current plotted rollups.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8325280/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; NCBI Bookshelf/PubMed RCT evidence summaries; PubMed RCT records; ClinicalTrials.gov where trial-registry facts are used","reason":"The current evidence_sources field names DailyMed and non-whitelisted epilepsy organization sources. The retained row facts should cite trusted source domains from the audit policy.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2000/20789lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK327367/bin/appl-et1.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21166480/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA accessdata labeling","reason":"Mechanism facts are supported by FDA labeling; cite FDA accessdata rather than DailyMed to stay within trusted-source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/214273s000lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb; published=Oct 03, 2025; title=ZONEGRAN (ZONISAMIDE) CAPSULE [ADVANZ PHARMA (US) CORP.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb; effective_time=20250912; title=Zonegran / ZONISAMIDE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for black-box verification; use FDA/openFDA metadata.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22d12de43e-3ac3-4335-bc85-70d7366a91eb%22&limit=5"]}],"summary":"Zonisamide row needs updates. The RCT links and RR50/MPC efficacy rollups are mostly supported, but seizure-freedom is not NR because Lu2011 reports 3/52 vs 1/50. FDA source handling needs cleanup, especially black-box warning source. The max approved daily dose, mechanism filter, evidence_sources, QT wording, generalized seizure-type claims, and some adverse-event wording require correction or added trusted sources."}
